   "rule_summary": "Manufacturers must report any thermal incident involving fire, smoke, uncontrolled overheating, or emergency evacuation to the responsible regulator within 24 hours of becoming aware of it, with a complete incident report within 10 business days. They must notify affected customers and, where there is a credible risk to nearby people or property, relevant local emergency authorities within 72 hours.",
   "comparison": "all parameters acceptable or better",
   "final_rule_text": "## S1_incident_reporting\nManufacturers must report any thermal incident involving fire, smoke, uncontrolled overheating, or emergency evacuation to the responsible regulator within 24 hours of becoming aware of it, with a complete incident report within 10 business days. They must notify affected customers and, where there is a credible risk to nearby people or property, relevant local emergency authorities within 72 hours. Reports must include known circumstances, model and serial number, injuries or property damage, and immediate safety steps. Manufacturers must maintain incident records and report annually, including incidents initially determined not to be product-related."
  },
