   "comparison": "weakened by: over_limit_consequence",
   "final_rule_text": "Each model must undergo a sustained-heat test at 55 °C using a regulator-approved protocol, a representative sample, and documented results. The maximum permitted failure rate is 5% per model. Manufacturers must submit each model’s results, including sample size and exact failure rate, to the responsible regulator and independent conformity assessor. Before purchase, customers must receive a safety-relevant summary stating whether the model meets the limit and describing any required corrective actions; exact per-model failure rates and sample sizes are not customer-facing. A model exceeding the limit must be investigated, corrective action documented, and retested on a regulator-approved schedule. Exceeding the limit requires regulator oversight and proportionate interim safeguards, but does not by itself require market withdrawal or a ban."
